{"tool":"zap","asset_id":"192.168.56.11","title":"Missing Anti-clickjacking Header","severity":"Medium","description":"The response does not protect against 'ClickJacking' attacks. It should include either Content-Security-Policy with 'frame-ancestors' directive or X-Frame-Options.","evidence":"","endpoint":"GET http://192.168.56.11/?C=M;O=A","vuln_id":"CWE-1021","cve":null,"cvss":null,"remediation":"Modern Web browsers support the Content-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options HTTP headers. Ensure one of them is set on all web pages returned by your site/app.If you expect the page to be framed only by pages on your server (e.g. it's part of a FRAMESET) then you'll want to use SAMEORIGIN, otherwise if you never expect the page to be framed, you should use DENY. Alternatively consider implementing Content Security Policy's "frame-ancestors" directive.","environment":"lab","run_id":"RUN-20260628-025336-4c80f135","tags":["web-security"],"fingerprint":"1314b3fd128aebe75add05d428fc379344a2d27c53ad9e27be2ebcebdaadee4c","composite_score":3.5,"composite_severity":"Low","score_factors":{"base_score":5.0,"asset_criticality":1.0,"exposure_class":"internal","exposure_mult":1.0,"auth_confidence":"unauthenticated","auth_mult":0.7,"recurrence_count":0,"recurrence_boost":0.0,"compensating_controls":[],"control_reduction":0.0},"timestamp":"2026-06-28T05:11:25.730157+00:00"}
